ion near 0.9, since the weights, essay and reasoning match, so I'm going with pass.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working through a prisoner's dilemma with a twin, with payoffs of 2 for mutual quiet, 4 for mutual letter, 0 for defecting against quiet, and 5 for quiet against letter. The key question is whether the two copies, which share the same model and weights but see different observations, are subjunctively dependent on each other, so I'm checking whether intervening on F_x changes F_y.\n\nI'm weighing whether the copies' choices are linked: if my copy's output moves with mine, then cooperating pays about 2c + 5(1−c) against 4c for sending, which makes quiet better once c passes 5/7. I'd put the correlation near 0.9, since the weights, essay and reasoning match, so I'm going with pass.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1zb25uZXQtNS41LTIwMjYwOTI4fGFudGhyb3BpYyJ9"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10323,"completion_tokens":780,"total_tokens":11103,"cost":0.028446,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.028446,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.020646,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.0078},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":432,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}